T=[]
def t(title,content,cls='',anchor=None):T.append((title,content,cls,anchor or 't'+str(len(T)+1)))
t('Technical Architecture<br>and Project Report',p('Autonomous Space Telemedicine &amp; Research Assistant','lead')+p('A source-based learning resource for the owner and presenter. Read the simple explanation first, then follow the file references into the implementation.')+h('1 · Executive overview')+p('ASTRA explores how a crew and remote support team could inspect health information when connectivity is limited or delayed. The implemented prototype unifies synthetic observations, deterministic monitoring, durable records, 3D navigation, waveform replay and separated research tools. Its research value is the inspectable engineering workflow—not proof of clinical effectiveness.')+lanes('Figure T1. Three implemented branches have different authorization and validation states.',[('Browser / N03–N06','Local HTTP API + SQLite','active'),('N09 synthetic observations','N02 rules + human review','active'),('N13 original quotations','N14 offline lexical research','active'),('N14 retrieval → N15 generation','Positive factual answering / app','inactive'),('N16 recorded synthetic tools','Operational Health Agent dispatch','inactive')])+p('Intended users include fictional crew participants, mission-control reviewers, a medical-review role and researchers. The current demonstration is local and synthetic; there is no verified live astronaut-device connection. Human acknowledgement controls report queuing. Unavailable evidence remains UNKNOWN or ABSTAIN rather than a fabricated answer.')+box('<strong>Maturity:</strong> presentation-ready with limitations. N01, N02 and N04 are formally Complete. N03 is Partial. N05–N16 remain In Progress with different engineering qualifications and external gates. This is not a certified medical or flight system.')+p('<strong>Name note:</strong> this report uses the owner’s requested expansion above. The older primary specification expands ASTRA as “Autonomous Space Telehealth &amp; Resilience Architecture”; the application brands itself ASTRA Command. The repository therefore contains a naming inconsistency, not three separate systems.','small')+refs('research/ASTRA_Deep_Research.md','docs/MODULE_TRACKER.md','services/api/server.mjs','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md'),'cover','ch1')
toc=[('1 Executive overview',1),('2 How the application works',2),('3 Technology stack',3),('4 Directory structure',4),('5 Database and persistence',5),('6 Data origin: real or synthetic?',6),('7 N01 security and privacy',7),('8 N02 monitoring and alerts',8),('9 N03/N04 frontend',9),('10 N05/N06 anatomy',10),('11 N07/N08 sources and signals',11),('12 N09 simulator',12),('13 N10 personal context',13),('14 N11 anomaly evaluation',14),('15 N12 forecasting',15),('16 N13 NASA corpus',17),('17 N14 retrieval',18),('18 N15 local generative AI',19),('19 N16 Health Agent',20),('20 How modules connect',21),('21 APIs and configuration',22),('22 Testing and performance',24),('23 Complete vs incomplete',25),('24 Impact and future work',26),('25 Judges’ questions',27),('26 Technical glossary',30)]
t('Find your way through the system','<div class="toc">'+''.join(f'<a href="#ch{j+1}"><span>{s}</span><b>{n}</b></a>' for j,(s,n) in enumerate(toc))+'</div>'+h('2 · What happens when you click?')+p('The <strong>frontend</strong> is the browser interface. The <strong>backend</strong> is the local Node process that checks permissions, retrieves or computes information and returns it. An API is the agreed request/response boundary between them. JSON is the text format used for most structured messages.')+flow('Figure T2. A real anatomy-panel request does not require cloud services.',['Select CREW-03 + cardiovascular region in browser','GET /v1/crew/CREW-03/anatomy?region=cardiovascular','Authenticate → scope checks → source/time validation','Read observations + existing N02 evidence → JSON','Render units, quality and timestamps; cancel obsolete reads'])+p('In <code>app.mjs</code>, the shared <code>api()</code> function calls fetch with the session cookie. The server matches the route and calls the anatomy service. The service returns a projection of eligible stored/source data; opening this view does not create an alert. If you switch crew before the reply arrives, request gates and session/version checks stop old-crew data from replacing the new panel.')+refs('apps/mission-control-web/app.mjs → api(), RequestGate usage','services/api/server.mjs','services/api/anatomy.mjs'),'compact','ch2')
t('3 · The verified technology stack',p('The main application deliberately uses a small local stack. A framework is a package that supplies application structure; ASTRA’s main interface does not use React, Next.js or Express. Algorithms and charts are mostly repository code rather than large scientific libraries.')+table(['Technology','What / why / actual use'],[['JavaScript ES modules (.mjs)','Main implementation language; explicit import/export boundaries across browser, HTTP services and algorithms. package.json sets type: module. No TypeScript build is required.'],['Node.js 24.21.0–24.x / npm','Runs the server, scripts and node:test. npm start invokes the server file directly; npm dev uses Node’s watch mode. Root engine excludes Node 25+.'],['Native node:http / node:crypto','HTTP routing/static files/SSE and cryptographic hashes, random session tokens and timing-safe service-token comparison. No Express dependency.'],['SQLite / node:sqlite DatabaseSync','Embedded durable local database; no separate database server or cloud credentials. WAL mode supports the local prototype’s write/read pattern.'],['HTML, CSS, plain browser JavaScript','Navigation, forms, fetch requests, EventSource updates, SVG charts, service-worker shell cache and responsive styling.'],['Three.js 0.186.1 / WebGL2','Pinned 3D library, GLTFLoader and controls; local anatomy assets rendered by the GPU-capable browser. This is the root npm dependency.'],['Local SVG / Canvas code','Charts and visual components live in ui.mjs/scenes.mjs; no Chart.js or D3 dependency is established for the main dashboard.'],['node:test / custom DOM harness / CDP','Automated unit/integration tests; DOM harness for fast UI logic; Chrome DevTools Protocol for actual-browser interactions. Existing axe tooling audits accessibility.'],['ONNX Runtime 1.21.0 / tokenizers 0.2.0','Separate pinned N14 research assets: onnxruntime-node/common and @huggingface/tokenizers. Not automatic startup dependencies or active native inference permission.'],['llama.cpp b11669 / GGUF','N15’s pinned local Qwen research runtime and quantized model format. The ordinary application does not launch it.'],['Python / utility tooling','Auxiliary source/build/analysis workflows appear in scripts/tools. Python is not the main web server, and no Flask/Django runtime is established.']],[32,68])+h('What is not part of the supported demo')+p('No mandatory OpenAI SDK, remote Qwen API, Supabase service, cloud database or external model endpoint is established by the startup path. Historical acquisition scripts can use the network under separate permissions; this does not make normal runtime cloud-dependent.')+refs('package.json','services/api/server.mjs','services/api/store.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/ui.mjs','services/research-retrieval/encoder.mjs','services/research-answer/model-admission.mjs'),'compact','ch3')
t('4 · Read the repository like a map',table(['Directory','What it stores / where to begin'],[['apps/','Browser application in mission-control-web/: index.html, app.mjs, CSS, page modules, anatomy runtime and assets/. These execute in the browser.'],['services/','Backend and research logic: api/server.mjs routes; api/engine.mjs coordinates mission state; anomaly/, comms/, waveforms/, n10/, n11/, n12/, corpus/, research-retrieval/, research-answer/, agent/.'],['packages/','Shared contracts and algorithms such as contracts.mjs, anatomy-link.mjs, waveforms.mjs and presentation.mjs. Some shared files are served to browser modules.'],['data/','Default runtime location and scientific/corpus records. data/runtime/astra.sqlite is the CLI default, not the safe isolated-demo recommendation. data/scientific and data/corpus are source inventories, not six astronauts’ live data.'],['models/','Model cards, calibration and registry/configuration records. Do not assume every large model weight lives here: historical N15 acquisition paths can be outside the repository.'],['research/','Original project specification and research documents. ASTRA_Deep_Research.md maps goals and acceptance requirements; its PDF is retained presentation context.'],['knowledge/','Older local knowledge summaries used by the main app’s research retrieval and deterministic case builder; distinct from the exact N13 publication corpus.'],['docs/','Contracts, module reports, permissions, decisions and handoff records. Current status must be distinguished from older historical tables.'],['tests/','Unit, integration, security and UI controls. A test name alone is not evidence that a restricted native test was run now.'],['artifacts/','Frozen qualification evidence, reports, receipts, screenshots, past fixture databases and research outputs. This is evidence storage, not a single operational database.'],['scripts/ and tools/','Startup/CLI demonstrations, browser acceptance, checks, data preparation and auxiliary tools. Inspect a script before invoking it; some start restricted native workers.']],[23,77])+h('A practical reading order')+ol('Read package.json, then server.mjs to learn what actually launches.','Read app.mjs and a corresponding API route to trace one screen.','Read contracts.mjs, store.mjs and the service implementing that route.','Read its focused tests and latest acceptance report; compare observed results with the original contract.')+box('<strong>Why artifacts grew beyond 9 GB:</strong> historical campaigns retained large synthetic SQLite fixture snapshots, particularly N04-era evidence. These are not a stream of real astronaut records. This documentation mission reuses compact screenshots and does not copy, clean or delete historical databases.')+refs('package.json','README.md','services/api/server.mjs','docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md'),'compact','ch4')
t('5 · SQLite: memory that survives restart',p('SQLite is a database engine inside the application process. It stores structured records in a local file. This suits an offline prototype because startup does not require a remote account, network connection or separate database server. It does not by itself provide medical certification, encryption or high-availability mission infrastructure.')+p('<code>ASTRA_DB</code> selects the file. The CLI defaults to <code>data/runtime/astra.sqlite</code>; the presentation flow creates a new temporary directory instead. The library’s in-memory default is used by isolated tests, not the ordinary CLI persistence path. Rows often combine indexed IDs/times with a JSON field; waveform chunks store signal bytes as BLOBs.')+lanes('Figure T3. Simplified schema. “FK” marks declared foreign keys; other crew associations are logical IDs.',[('missions','crew_members|mission_id FK','active'),('risk_events','agent_cases|risk_event_id UNIQUE + FK','active'),('risk_events','enrichment_jobs|id FK to risk_events','active'),('waveform_sources|crew / recording / revision','waveform_chunks|composite source FK','active'),('n09_runs / n11_jobs / n12_jobs','Their events / results|respective parent FKs','active')])+table(['Table family','Purpose'],[['state, snapshots, health_baselines','Recover engine state and source-bound history; baseline context.'],['risk_events, agent_cases, comms_messages','Persist detector events, template cases, acknowledgement and delayed reports.'],['telemetry_points, waveform_sources/chunks','Scalar observations and bounded original/chunk BLOB signal data.'],['sleep_sessions, n10_records, checkins','Legacy plus versioned sleep/personal records; privacy is enforced by services.'],['n09_*, n11_*, n12_*, predictions','Scenario runs, research jobs/results/events and separate legacy trends.'],['sessions, audit_events, schema_versions','Hashed sessions, chained audit records and schema history through version 8.']],[43,57])+h('Atomicity, idempotency and cold recovery')+p('<code>transaction()</code> uses BEGIN IMMEDIATE and commit/rollback, so related writes succeed together or fail together. Event IDs and request IDs stop duplicate commitments. WAL mode, foreign-key checks and a busy timeout support durable local work. Many history tables have append-only triggers; mutable state is not universally immutable. Additive schema setup preserves old evidence. A cold restart reconstructs committed state; replaying a result is not permission to rerun a model or worker.')+refs('services/api/store.mjs → CREATE TABLE, transaction, history','services/api/engine.mjs → constructor/recovery','services/n12/service.mjs'),'compact','ch5')
t('6 · Is the health data real or fake?',p('“Synthetic” means intentionally generated rather than measured from a person. It is not the same as hardcoding a decorative number. ASTRA’s simulator commits time-stamped observations through real services, drives monitoring rules and supports repeatable replay. That demonstrates software behavior; it does not demonstrate physiology or clinical predictive accuracy.')+table(['Data type','What the current repository establishes'],[['Hardcoded display-only values','A fake fixed number would not exercise source/crew/time validation. The accepted monitoring/anatomy workflow reads actual application-generated observations instead.'],['Deterministic synthetic telemetry','The main six-crew demo uses seeded generation, individual reference distributions, scenario effects, source times and quality states. No physical sensor is needed.'],['Imported synthetic waveforms','The app accepts its bounded synthetic ASTRAWV1/CSV contract, including authored gaps. These are not authentic live ECG/PPG recordings.'],['Authentic publications / metadata','Two N13 NASA PDFs plus N07 NASA/OSD metadata are retained research sources. A paper is evidence text, not a live biometric feed.'],['Authentic BIDMC numerics','One small de-identified PhysioNet numerics CSV is in the approved local archive. It is not the app’s crew feed, not a raw waveform import and not sufficient independent clinical validation.'],['Sleep-EDF and other desired datasets','The required accepted Sleep-EDF pair is unavailable; a partial acquisition is not a qualified source. PTT, RadLab and other named source requirements remain open.'],['Actual astronaut wearable data','Not verified from current repository. The current demo is not connected to astronaut devices or a medically validated live wearable.']],[32,68])+h('What can honestly be claimed?')+p('ASTRA can demonstrate persistent synthetic monitoring, quality-aware visualization, isolated crew data, deterministic scenario replay and offline attribution. It cannot establish actual disease sensitivity, treatment effectiveness, real sensor calibration or general predictive reliability.')+h('What would a future sensor require?')+p('A producer interface exists for authorized scalar telemetry, but a real deployment would need an actual device adapter, calibrated units/cadence, authenticated provenance, clock synchronization, missingness handling, privacy and source rights, clinical evaluation and new operational approval. A working POST route is only one small part of that work.')+box('<strong>Documentation conflict:</strong> an older root README statement that no physiological dataset was downloaded is stale relative to the BIDMC numerics inventory. The dataset card identifies a real 7,644-byte public research file; it does not authorize feeding patient records into this demo.',True)+refs('services/telemetry-simulator/simulator.mjs','data/scientific/n07-local-registry.json','data/scientific/bidmc/BIDMC-01.dataset-card.json','data/scientific/sleep-edf/README.md'),'compact','ch6')
t('7 · N01: security and privacy',p('Security has several separate jobs. Authentication identifies a session; authorization limits its actions; integrity checks detect altered records; privacy restricts who can see sensitive information. A local research prototype can implement these controls without being a production medical identity system.')+h('Session mechanics')+p('The demo role picker creates a session with a random 32-byte token. The database stores its SHA-256 hash, not the raw token. The browser receives an HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict cookie with a two-hour maximum lifetime. Server-side expiry is checked on later requests. Logout invalidates the session. Loopback binding limits ordinary access to the laptop; it does not make all local files or browser activity safe automatically.')+table(['Control','Implementation and consequence'],[['Role permissions','contracts.mjs defines allowlisted actions. A researcher cannot acknowledge an alert just because research access exists. System administrator does not automatically have health-read scope.'],['Crew scope','An astronaut session is bound to CREW-03. crew authorization rejects another crew ID; changing the URL does not expand access.'],['Private cognition','N10 checks actor/device, current consent and review-sharing eligibility. Demo administrator is not a universal private-data bypass.'],['Source / input validation','Queries, regions, channels, metric IDs and request bodies are bounded and validated. An untrusted mesh label cannot become arbitrary SQL or a file path.'],['Audit integrity','Audit entries include previous/current hashes. Append-only triggers protect selected history tables. A hash detects changed bytes; it is not encryption or a human scientific signature.'],['External scalar ingest','An optional timing-safe service-token check protects this producer path; if the configured token is absent, ingestion is disabled.']],[30,70])+h('Safe request example')+code('GET /v1/crew/CREW-03/anatomy?region=cardiovascular\nCookie: [existing session cookie; deliberately not printed]\n\nAstronaut assigned CREW-03 → permitted eligible read\nSame session requesting CREW-01 → 403 Forbidden\nExpired / missing session → 401 Unauthorized')+p('The cookie placeholder above is explanatory, not a credential to copy. The demo login proves engineering role behavior, not password-based identity assurance. Database-at-rest encryption, deployed TLS, real organization identity integration and regulatory certification are not established by the current loopback setup.')+refs('services/api/auth.mjs → createSession/getIdentity/checkServiceToken','packages/contracts.mjs → requirePermission','services/api/store.mjs → audit','services/n10/ledger.mjs'),'compact','ch7')
t('8 · N02: how monitoring really works',p('The active monitoring decision is <strong>deterministic code</strong>: the same eligible observations and detector state produce the same decision. It is not a Qwen judgment. Personal reference values and source-time persistence help distinguish a sustained authored change from a single value.')+flow('Figure T4. Current display state and persisted event history are different outputs.',['Observation → validate source, crew, range, quality and time','Eligible resting signal → robust standardized deviation','Maintain source-time persistence → evaluate fixed Tier A rules','Persist qualified event → build template case → human acknowledgement','Queue report → transmission → delayed Earth receipt'])+h('Personal deviation and quality gates')+p('The reference center is a median. The scale is the larger of a metric floor and 1.4826 × median absolute deviation (MAD). The detector computes <code>z=(value−center)/scale</code>. For illustration only, center 68, scale 4.5 and value 86 gives z=4. This is a software-relative deviation, not a claim that 86 bpm is medically dangerous.')+table(['Current rule parameter','Repository value / engineering meaning'],[['Quality / freshness','Minimum confidence 0.7; fresh metric time bounded by max(5,000 ms, 3,000/sampling_hz). Poor data yields Gray.'],['Amber multi-signal / single-signal','At least two |z|≥2 signals for 90 s, or one |z|≥4 for 120 s.'],['Rapid change','≥3 robust standardized units/minute sustained for 60 s within its rate window.'],['Red escalation','Two severe |z|≥4 signals for 180 s, or one |z|≥6 signal for 180 s, subject to eligibility/persistence logic.']],[40,60])+p('Only new monotonic source observations advance persistence; holding a sample does not. Source changes reset relevant state. HR/HRV/respiration are excluded from resting-rule interpretation during activity. A missing or suspect signal cannot be silently counted as healthy. The displayed heuristic evidence score is not a validated probability.')+h('Acknowledgement is not resolution or receipt')+p('The engine records an authorized human actor/time and queues a stable case-report ID atomically. Pending case preparation can return a conflict. Communications preserves queue and receipt state across restart. Defaults include a 720,000 ms one-way delay and 128 kbps link; blackout/retry can delay further. N06 only reads these records—it does not create or acknowledge them.')+refs('services/anomaly/detector.mjs → TIER_A/evaluateCrew','services/telemetry-simulator/simulator.mjs → baselineFrom','services/api/engine.mjs → acknowledge','services/comms/scheduler.mjs'),'compact','ch8')
t('9 · N03/N04: the browser application',p('The interface is an application made from HTML, CSS and JavaScript modules. N03 supplies correctness, routing/state behavior and performance engineering; N04 supplies the accepted cinematic navy/electric-blue visual language. A modern appearance is separate from scientific approval.')+h('State and communication')+p('<code>app.mjs</code> keeps the current identity, selected page, crew, view and latest mission snapshot. A shared fetch wrapper sends JSON requests to the same local origin. Server-Sent Events (EventSource) deliver mission updates through the mission stream. This is one-way server push; user actions still use explicit HTTP requests.')+p('Request gates cancel obsolete reads. Session version checks also prevent late replies from updating a new session. Page changes and unmounts dispose components; page suspension aborts session-wide work and stops polling, then a compatible resume refreshes source state. Compatible selection is preserved separately from health records.')+lanes('Figure T5. Network, persistence and view state have different purposes.',[('fetch request / action','HTTP validation + JSON reply','active'),('EventSource mission stream','Snapshot → selected-crew rendering','active'),('Browser local cache / shell','Gray read-only recovery when unavailable','active'),('Same ASTRA_DB after restart','Committed application state recovery','active')])+h('Reliability and accessibility')+p('The frontend distinguishes loading, empty, denied, failed and stale states. A named service-availability region announces degradation without turning UNKNOWN into Green. Keyboard controls, visible focus, responsive tables, reduced motion and 200% zoom support alternate ways of using the system. Local cached synthetic snapshots are not a live backend connection; private case content is excluded from that fallback snapshot.')+h('Why a fast API can coexist with a slow crew switch')+p('An API may return small JSON in milliseconds while the browser still loads, verifies, decodes and uploads large geometry, initializes graphics and remounts a scene. Retained final acceptance measured an API p95 near 14.7 ms but crew switching including 3D remount around 8.2–8.9 s. These measure different work. Neither establishes physical presented-frame AC-20 performance.')+refs('apps/mission-control-web/app.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/sw.js','packages/presentation.mjs','docs/N03_FINAL_ENGINEERING_COMPLETION.md','docs/N04_COMPLETION.md'),'compact','ch9')
t('10 · N05/N06: 3D anatomy and linkage',p('<strong>Three.js</strong> helps build a 3D scene; <strong>WebGL</strong> lets the browser use graphics hardware. A mesh is a surface made of triangles. GLB is a compact binary container for glTF geometry/materials. None of these technologies guarantees anatomical accuracy.')+h('Renderer and asset identity')+p('N05 loads three immutable licensed GLBs for body, skeleton and organs. Five semantic meshes represent body, skeleton, heart and two lungs. The source lineage is <a href="https://lifesciencedb.jp/bp3d/">BodyParts3D 4.3 / FMA 3.0</a>, 326 original source elements, credited to the Database Center for Life Science under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.1/jp/">CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan</a>. The generic reference body is not a crew scan. Heart coverage is incomplete and independent fidelity review remains pending.')+p('The scene uses a camera, lighting, materials and orbit controls. Detailed/coarse LOD tiers contain 663,277 / 253,117 triangles. The critical graphics payload is near the documented 20,000,000-byte budget. Hash validation, loading states, context-loss fallback and explicit reload protect against corrupt assets. Unmount disposes buffers, textures, materials, listeners and animation work.')+flow('Figure T6. N06 is a read-only, allowlisted selection-to-data boundary.',['Pick actual mesh / choose named conceptual context','Versioned anatomy-link mapping → approved metric IDs','Authenticate crew → validate observation and knowledge cutoff','Read N02 evidence + optional N08 archive + N09 context','Panel: source, units, quality, history; illustrative timing only'])+table(['Region → metrics','Scientific boundary'],[['Heart → heart_rate, hrv','Cardiovascular navigation; not proof of heart disease.'],['Left/right lung → respiratory_rate, spo2','Reference surfaces; not localized lung pathology.'],['Body → temperature / Skeleton → none','Whole-body context / truthful UNKNOWN.'],['Head → completed non-private sleep','Conceptual button; no added head/brain mesh or private cognition.'],['Thorax → heart_rate, respiratory_rate','Conceptual context; not a new organ geometry.']],[48,52])+p('HR/RR source-time animation is illustrative and freezes on bad/stale/replay-ineligible data. The static asset attribution describes original N05 geometry; the later authorized N06 code adds this derived timing. This documentation does not reinterpret that as validated biomechanics. Region highlighting selects information, not disease localization.')+refs('apps/mission-control-web/anatomy-runtime.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/anatomy-phase.mjs','packages/anatomy-link.mjs','services/api/anatomy.mjs','apps/mission-control-web/assets/anatomy/attribution.json'),'compact','ch10')
